WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.480
God, you're so pathetic.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.990
You've gotta pick up
the pace on these laps, man.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.750
Or we'll <i>both</i> be late.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.330
I just can't run anymoreвЂ”

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.340
Hey!

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.090
S-Sorry!

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.130
Ew! Don't get handsy!

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.680
You know I'm only here because
you said you wanted to retrain, right?

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.560
Show a little effort.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.900
I'm pretty sure I just asked you to
teach me some self-defense moves.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:51.650
Learning a few fancy moves wouldn't be much like you.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.570
You need guts.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.240
So no matter how many times
you get hit, you don't go down.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.280
An indomitable spirit.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:59.370
Ow!

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.370
We're gonna be working
at JNR together, right?

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.000
Huh?

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.620
So show me your guts.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.710
You gonna be okay with that?

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:15.930
It's got less parts than the timebomb.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.720
Wow, really?

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.180
Please!

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.890
I'm talking about safety!

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:22.020
Worry about yourself.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:23.270
Ow!

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.890
That's only a temporary treatment.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.520
Make sure you go to the doctor's later.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.320
This is the best!

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.440
The tea's ready!

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.280
So you can do more than just break things, huh, Sakurai?

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.490
Maintenance is part of the basics.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.410
My dad really whipped that into me.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:48.120
Maybe I should prove to you I'm great at massages, too.

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.420
Don't put humans and guns
on the same level.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:53.670
Here.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.170
Thanks, Koumi.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.590
What?

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.770
Oh, it's nothing.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:10.400
I'm not really a fan of princes.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.650
Girls are usually into that stuff.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:15.820
Like Cinderella and whatnot.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:16.940
What?

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.200
I'll sum up that story for you: girl goes dancing at a castle,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.490
it's love at first sight,
she and the prince get married.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:29.330
What's so great about a story where the girl has to rely on a man to live happily ever after?

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:34.340
Besides, if someone dressed like that
held me close, I'd die of embarrassment.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.470
Whatever guy tries to seduce you, Sakurai, is in for a lot of pain.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.850
Wh-What?

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.400
Nothing.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.990
Thank you for waiting.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:36.500
The 7:03pm Limited Express Sleeping Car Hokutosei #3
bound for Sapporo will be arriving on line 13 momentarily.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:41.960
For your safety, please stay behind the yellow line.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.970
The train is entering from the left side.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.510
Those taking pictures, please make room.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:03.360
The lead electric
locomotive is an EF81.

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:07.110
Hokutosei #3 is made up of 12 cars.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:11.330
The engine is followed by the generator car, after which come car 11, car 10, and so on.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:19.790
Cars 1 through 5 are Type B bedrooms, with bunk beds and private rooms.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:20.840
Car 6 is...

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.340
...the lounge car, right?

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.340
Everyone can use it, and it has a couch and shower room.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:28.180
Car 7 is the dining car.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:31.310
And cars 8 through 10 are Type A deluxe rooms!

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:34.270
And the last car is another Type B.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.270
I know all about it!

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.150
I told myself I had to ride it
if I ever came to this country!

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.320
That's dangerous, Prince Bernina!

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.320
So this is the EF81...

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.490
It's even better than I imagined!

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.700
Why does it have a generator car?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.410
They can just get power from the overhead lines.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:57.790
Some areas of the Hokkaido Line aren't electrified.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.920
It acts as a power supply to get through those sections.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:09.010
More specifically, the generator car of the Hokutosei is equipped with a KaNi24 large-type diesel generator.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:19.270
I heard that the DF51, the greatest diesel engine on
narrow-gauge railways, runs on the non-electrified sections.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.270
That's so great! I just gotta see that!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:25.650
The JNR engines have
a special place in my heart.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.280
I can't pick a favorite!

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.780
You sure get it.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:35.620
There's the EF68, a new electric locomotive that pulls the Hayabusa and Fuji sleeper trains.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.290
And, and...

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.540
You can't forget the EF63.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.960
Nicknamed the "Sherpa of Mountain Pass"!

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.960
You're a railway fan too, huh?

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:48.550
Ciao, Takayama!

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.090
I've shown the prince to his Royal room.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.510
Koumi is with him.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.060
Sakurai went to the Ueno PSF office.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:06.610
As I explained today, the prince will be getting to the
sister city ceremony in Sapporo tomorrow via the 7:03 train.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:10.860
You are to guide and assist him along the way.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:11.570
Right.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:15.950
And just like usual, keep relaxed.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:19.620
Don't hesitate to do what you think is right.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.580
I'll take responsibility.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.080
Ma'am!

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:26.090
I'll be waiting for you
guys to come home.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.130
Yes?

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.090
Oh, Takayama.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:35.100
Haruka's just been going
on and on about you.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.970
What were you talking about, Your Highness?

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.560
Call me Bernina.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:43.520
We both love the rails.
I want us to be friends!

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.070
Then you can call me Naoto.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.030
Okay, Naoto!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.030
You're really good at Japanese, Bernina.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:55.030
Haruka taught me a whole lot way back.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.040
Oh?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:04.040
When you're done changing, let us know.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.250
Wow, Koumi.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:11.970
Having a prince as your friend is surprise enough, but he actually requested you specifically.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:12.930
He must really trust youвЂ”

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:17.300
Bernina and I were classmates
when I studied abroad in England.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.100
Really, that's all.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.230
Oh, okay.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.690
Well, I'm gonna go call
Sakurai and Iwaizumi.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.770
I'm not lying.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.250
That's the last of the bags.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.960
Thanks.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.580
Sakurai, where are you?

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.420
I spotted someone suspicious.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.880
In a black suit, with sunglasses on.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:53.880
He was watching the Hokutosei, but when he realized I was looking at him, he fled. I'm chasing him now!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.340
He's putting up a fight!
I'm taking this bastard in!

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.350
What are you talking about?
The train's gonna leave!

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.480
I swear I'll catch him!

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:05.350
It's my job to protect you.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:06.770
Sakurai?

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.730
The doors are closing.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.940
Paging line #3's driver, over.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:17.030
Yes, this is line #3's driver, over.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.780
Line #3, clear to leave.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.740
Roger. Line #3 leaving station.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.430
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:48.850
This is the 7:03 Hokutosei #3
from Ueno bound for Sapporo.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:53.150
I'm Yamada from the JNR Sendai Railway Administration, and I'll be your driver today.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.700
Now, these are our stops and arrival times.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.740
Omiya, 7:28 p.m.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.410
Utsunomiya, 8:27 p.m.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.990
Koriyama, 9:52 p.m.

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:06.210
Fukushima, 10:27 p.m.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.170
Sendai, 11:27 p.m.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:12.250
After Sendai we will stop in Hakodate.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:15.380
That's tomorrow morning, 6:34 a.m.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.470
Then Mori, 7:26 a.m.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.180
Yakumo, 8:05 a.m.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.390
Oshamanbe, 8:29 a.m.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:21.760
What's Sakurai going to do?

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.220
Toya, 8:59 a.m.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.020
Datemombetsu, 9:11 a.m.

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:38.950
Yes?

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.990
Takayama!

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:41.950
Where's Aoi?

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.200
She's taking a different route.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.540
Aoi's not here?

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.210
We can meet up on the way.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:51.130
Besides, we have Iwaizumi.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:52.710
You can count on me!

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.880
And you can take care of Bernina.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:58.220
Right.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.970
I'll do what I can, too.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.970
Okay, let's decide on rooms.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.980
So I just sit here on standby?

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.980
You sure I shouldn't be out
in front of the room?

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:21.490
You stick out too much. That'd just
telegraph to the enemy where the target is.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.530
Takayama, you think this guy's strong?

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:26.240
Try not to go overboard, please.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:29.250
No can do, Deputy!

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.710
I'm coming in, Koumi.

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:34.080
I-I'm sorry!

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:36.090
I-It's okay.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.260
You just surprised me.

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:44.010
I know this will be dangerous,
but I trust you, KoumiвЂ”

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.640
I'm a PSF member too, you know?

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:51.640
I've been learning some self-defense from Aoi, so I can be of some help...

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.480
I thought I'd copy Aoi, for mobility.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:01.990
You're just the bait, Koumi,
so you won't be fighting.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.660
You just have to act like the real thing.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:07.490
I'm not so sure I can.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:11.790
You're the most refined person I know.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.960
You're even a "princess" of sorts.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:19.550
Even if you're lying, thanks.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.340
Now all that's left is Bernina.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.350
Iwaizumi is in room 4.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:32.520
Koumi will be in room 11, where Bernina was supposed
to stay, and fool the enemy into thinking she's the prince.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:37.940
I'll be with Bernina in room 12
all night for protection.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.530
Who was that?

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.910
Bernina?

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.030
It's Naoto.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.160
Bernina!

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.130
No way, was that...

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.290
I spotted someone suspicious.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.590
In a black suit, with sunglasses on.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:06.510
What is this, a suspense thriller?
Who attacks another person on a train?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.970
Y-You really can't be here, sir.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.680
Authorized personnel only.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.810
P-Please don't touch that!

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.150
Stop that.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:22.400
Only railway staff are allowed in there.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.030
Really? I'd never seen the likes before, so I couldn't help myself.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.870
I'm sorry for the trouble.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:34.250
Please stop barging into random rooms.

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:36.540
Excuse me, sir?

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:39.420
Sir?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:42.670
Sasshou?

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:43.420
Huh?

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:44.880
Takayama!

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:45.720
What're you doing here?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.140
I was assigned here for job training.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.060
Bernina!

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.610
Sasshou, sorry!

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:06.200
I'll make him apologize later!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.910
I'm so jealous of you guys.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:19.420
You can just hop on one of these majestic trains and have them take you wherever you want to go.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:27.380
You guys are in training
to be employed at JNR, right?

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.880
That's right.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.390
I love the rails, after all.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:34.260
I want to be a train driver.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:36.730
A train driver, huh?

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.730
I wish I could do that.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:41.110
You're to be king, right?

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.270
You'll never have to worry about money or employment ever.

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.820
I'm jealous of <i>you.</i>

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:57.500
I'm only fifth in line to the throne, so as long as nothing terrible happens, I doubt I'll be crowned.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.040
Fifth, huh?

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:09.420
Can I take a shower?

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:10.930
Oh, sure.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.350
Don't you peep, now.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.560
Promise me.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:24.980
I'm not about to peep
on a guy showering.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:31.490
Pardon me.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.960
The person you are trying to reach either
has turned off their phone or is out of service.

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:52.680
Atela?

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:02.560
A car carrying the King of Atela and four members of the royal family was in an accident today.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:05.150
Their status is still unknown.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.480
I have to tell Bernina!

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:19.700
Wait, do I have the wrong room?

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.710
The doors look so similar I just walked right in!

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.710
Is this room 11?

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.890
N-Naoto.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:42.730
Hey! Bernina, you okay?

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:45.060
Y-Yeah...

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:47.020
Bernina! I'm coming in!

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:56.820
Hey, Bernina! Wake up!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:03.370
Come on, BerninaвЂ”

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.300
H-He's a she?!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.720
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.880
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.300
Just calm down, man.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.680
Calm down.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:24.060
She'll catch cold if she stays wet.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.620
I have to get Koumi.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:47.790
Naoto.

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:48.710
Don't.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.790
I'm okay.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:52.050
But...

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:57.220
I just felt dizzy for a second after seeing the news on my phone.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:59.510
About the accident?

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:03.220
I was worried about my family.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.230
Then...

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.730
I'm sure they're safe!

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:12.440
Yeah.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.190
Thanks, Naoto.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.280
Naoto.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:21.330
You saw, didn't you?

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:23.580
Y-Yeah.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.750
Sorry.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:28.710
Only a select few of the
royal family know this secret.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.040
I haven't even told Haruka.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:32.790
Huh?

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.880
I'm sorry for hiding it.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:40.430
Will you keep it a secret?

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:43.430
S-Sure.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:45.520
Thanks.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:49.640
Takayama! Did something happen?

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:51.150
Everything all right?

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:55.480
Here.

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:57.030
It smells wonderful.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.990
Is this okay? You're not open yet.

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.990
The chief said it was fine.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.970
Why didn't you invite Koumi?

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:22.510
I knocked on her room,
but she didn't respond.

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:24.470
I assumed she was asleep.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:26.060
That seems off.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.480
You really made a ruckus.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:30.440
She must have heard it.

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.400
This is the Hokutosei #3 bound for Sapporo.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:40.570
Huh? But the dining car's closed.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:44.120
We're running on time.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:46.990
The next stop is Hakodate. Again, Hakodate.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.750
He's totally looking for a fight!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:49.750
The next stop is Hakodate. Again, Hakodate.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:55.290
We will arrive in Hakodate at approximately 6:34 a.m.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.500
What's going on?

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:01.590
Deputy, it looks like this guy's after us!

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.930
Actually, more like he's after the prince.

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:07.390
We're just to be disposed of.

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:08.970
Takayama!

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.140
Hide!

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:13.020
Don't injure him, Iwaizumi.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.770
No can do, Deputy.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:16.860
I doubt I can hold back against this guy.

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:21.110
Thank you for riding with us today.

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:35.960
You okay?

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:37.920
Take the prince and run!

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:41.840
Taking two guys on while trying to protect you will be difficult.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:42.420
All right.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.380
No crazy stunts!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:48.140
This way, Bernina!

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:50.350
Not happening, bub!

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.110
We'll lock ourselves in
a Royal room. Hurry!

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.690
Bernina, in there!

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:03.900
But...

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:05.820
Hurry!

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.120
Stop it!

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.830
I'm not going down that easily!

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:24.260
Or my training instructor,
Sakurai, will shoot me!

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:35.600
Just stop it!

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.150
No!

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:38.610
Not BerninaвЂ”

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:53.040
Sakurai?

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:56.870
Not bad, Takayama.

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:02.590
Not bad, huh?

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:43.400
The JNR DF51 type diesel engine!

00:23:43.400 --> 00:23:46.020
Using the JNR DD51 type
as a base for the body,

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:49.740
it boasts two sets of three-axle trucks and
twin engines putting out 3000 horsepower!

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:51.700
It's a monster on narrow-gauge railways!

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:52.910
Hey!

00:23:52.910 --> 00:23:56.990
Monster or whatever, this thing's out of control!

00:23:56.990 --> 00:23:59.250
How do we stop it?!

00:23:59.250 --> 00:24:02.290
Takayama, fix this!

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:05.960
Rail Wars, Episode Eleven: Count Me In.

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:09.550
Don't worry. I swear I'll protect you!
